{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity","id":675469,"title":"Garou Nation vs Humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T11:26:14-07:00","id":675469,"title":"Garou Nation vs Humanity","content":"One of the most compelling aspects of Werewolf: the Apocalypse, in my opinion, is the inherent antagonism between the werewolf race and humanity; as well as the idea of werewolves hunting people. One of the function of the Garou, according to their beliefs and culture, is to act as the immune system of Gaia, eradicating corruption, yes? People in the setting of Werewolf are not always, but often seen as tainted by the Weaver or Wyrm; and most tribes have some sort of issue with humans as a whole. <br /> <br /> And, of course, there's the Red Talons, who are pretty open about their disdain of all things human. <br /> <br /> (Disclaimer: I realize there's a vast difference between the game advocating misantrophy and racism - which clearly isn't the case - and the fictional werewolf race, in character, harboring collective resentment directed against humans. This isn't a thread about Werewolf supporting racism, it's a thread about the Garou culture and morality - pretty dark stuff - and how to use these things in the concept of an actual game). <br /> <br /> What also comes to mind is the idea of role reversal, that I believe is explored in the books in great detail - werewolves treating humanity the way humanity treats nature and animals; where becoming a werewolf means switching sides on the Man vs. Nature conflict. <br /> <br /> Now, the reason I started this thread is to get advice and to discuss how to deal with this particular theme in the context of an actual game. What sort of stories and plot points evolve out of these aspects of the game? <br /> <br /> Thoughts? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:54:57-07:00","id":675567,"title":"","content":"Well hmmmn Seen many debates on this issue, some people get offended by the impergium, especialy when its approvingly depicted.<br /> <br /> <br /> One concern is the transition, book in 2nd and 3rd edition mentions this a bit... a Homid cub transitions from human values to those of the Garou and of his own tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:11:30-07:00","id":675656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity#post675469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the reason I started this thread is to get advice and to discuss how to deal with this particular theme in the context of an actual game. What sort of stories and plot points evolve out of these aspects of the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that really depends upon what your players are like. You can go to some very ugly places with this particular issue, so it really depends upon what the players as a group function like. If they're okay delving into very squishy questions of morality (like was genocide against whole cultures during the Impergium actually <i>morally defensible</i>), then go to town with it. On the other hand, if they like things more clear cut &quot;Good Guys vs. Bad Guys&quot; and don't want to go much deeper than that, maybe this isn't the best theme to play upon, since if you look at some of the threads, this can get <i>complicated</i>.<br /> <br /> I for one really bristle when somebody makes the statement that the Garou have some sort of divine right to do pretty much anything they want (including outright murdering innocent people -- because of the &quot;crimes&quot; of society, &quot;they're at war&quot;, or they're justified because they're predators). My view is that justifying such behavior as right and proper because, y'know, <i>Gaia</i>... is something that strikes me as incredibly shallow and reprehensible. If I were playing in a game where that's the default view -- I mean, like the &quot;moral of the story&quot; seems to reinforce that viewpoint, I very quickly wouldn't want to play anymore.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I tend to hold that much of the problems that the Garou now face (and endlessly b**** about) are practically direct consequences of the psychological harm done to the humans during the Impergium, and to a lesser extent, their dismissive, contemptuous attitude towards the human race in general. I'd love to play in a game where that theme gets some play -- but there's all sorts of people on this board who clearly would feel that the Garou being morally responsible for the current state of affairs in the World of Darkness (and by extension, <i>will</i> be responsible for the Apocalypse whenever it comes) is thematically, the equivalent of running your nails down a chalkboard.<br /> <br /> So in short, I'd advise actually talking to your players about how they like to see the Garou nation and its morality vis-a-vis the Impergium, War of Rage, etc. <i>before</i> delving into the bottomless pit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:57:24-07:00","id":675727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=675567#post675567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well hmmmn Seen many debates on this issue, some people get offended by the impergium, especialy when its approvingly depicted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let them be offended, it's a story. Within the context of said story, humans aren't exactly the best thing to happen to Gaia. Killing a lot of people is bad in real life, we all know that, mmkay? In a game... the Garou should let the blood flow, lest the Wyrm-feeding apes destroy creation.<br /> <br /> Edit: contrast the brutality of the Impergium with the imperative that homid Garou are meant to breed with humans- so that werewolves have a vested interest in protecting humanity. Humans are elevated from enemies and prey animals to lovers and children and parents. I think having both aspects in the texture of the backstory of WtA makes for interesting character interaction/story opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 09-23-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:57:03-07:00","id":675918,"title":"","content":"The old debate of are Garou heroes or monsters always comes back to this. From my perspective, the people who keep shoving left wing politics into the game setting keep trying to make the Garou heroes and keep attributing to them their version of politics. People who aren't as obsessed with left wing politics seem to be fine with allowing the Garou to be monsters as well as depicting positive attributes to their culture.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the tension between the positive aspects of the Garou and their monstrous aspects.<br /> <br /> The main thing to remember is that Garou, like vampires, have a Beast, and it comes out as well. They are predators and have the instincts of predators. It's just that unlike vampires, the Garou are meant to be predators, and therefore the game is not about werewolves &quot;losing&quot; their humanity. If anything, it is about them accepting their predatory nature, but finding a balance with their spiritual side (Rage and Gnosis) and doing what they are supposed to be doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:49:25-07:00","id":676729,"title":"","content":"I find the way the Impergium is described in revised is unsatisfactory. I can see how humans have been culled (and more on that later), but there it is implied that garou ruled over mankind - terrorizing it. Such behaviour I find atypical for the garou, for there is no serious and logical reason for them to have done so. If there was, why wouldn't it have been passed on in oral garou culture to today. If it was instincts, why aren't the instincts in the garou today?<br /> Culing, as with the agricultural term, makes sense. Not that the garou had any traits they wanted to be removed from the gene-pool, like breeders today do, when they cull their flock. But, to enforce some kind of Darwinism. Garou, being a force of nature humans had to deal with - not not really evil overlords oppressing them. That said, any village wouldn't be needed to constantly checked upon in the Stone Age. Coming to check on the humans every other year to kill the elderly and sick would probably enough.<br /> Also, the Dawn Times already had the Litanei and it forbids to hunt humans for food, so that couldn't have been a reason to kill humans.<br /> <br /> So, there is not legitimation to mistreat humans, besides culling in a responsible way, on the garou's side and there is no explanation why such a behaviour would have been told as what had happened in the Dawn times, until today. Also, not in a way where you still try to be proud of your Ancestors and a part of the people can even channel the ancestors.<br /> <br /> It is said, that there were metaphysical reasons to stop the culling - and it has been said, that Children of Gaia wanted the humans to be educated so the would not grow unchecked. The Pure Ones seem to have had that method working, while the other tribes failed massively in that undertaking, and brought their failure to the Pure ones...<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion, the Impergium should just be a time where humans were killed by garou when old and weak. The same that happens to any other animal - but with the humans it had a special meaning, since they weren't prey. It shouldn't be depicted as a garou tyranny.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> That said, the Impergium was only ended in one regard - the total number of humans. Besides that, the garou still go around and kill humans that were sickened by the Wyrm (mentally or physically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:15:28-07:00","id":676854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=676729#post676729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the way the Impergium is described in revised is unsatisfactory. I can see how humans have been culled (and more on that later), but there it is implied that garou ruled over mankind - terrorizing it. Such behaviour I find atypical for the garou, for there is no serious and logical reason for them to have done so. If there was, why wouldn't it have been passed on in oral garou culture to today. If it was instincts, why aren't the instincts in the garou today?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Crinos is a hell of a drug. It could also have been as simple as humans prostrating themselves and some Garou saying &quot;hey, this is pretty nice!&quot; Especially if they were born of those humans, and took their upbringing to be promise that they would eventually grow to a position of prominence and privilege, slaying monsters and coming back to reverent and tractable humans, the most attractive of whom they took as mates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Culing, as with the agricultural term, makes sense. Not that the garou had any traits they wanted to be removed from the gene-pool, like breeders today do, when they cull their flock. But, to enforce some kind of Darwinism. Garou, being a force of nature humans had to deal with - not not really evil overlords oppressing them. That said, any village wouldn't be needed to constantly checked upon in the Stone Age. Coming to check on the humans every other year to kill the elderly and sick would probably enough.<br /> Also, the Dawn Times already had the Litanei and it forbids to hunt humans for food, so that couldn't have been a reason to kill humans.<br /> <br /> So, there is not legitimation to mistreat humans, besides culling in a responsible way, on the garou's side and there is no explanation why such a behaviour would have been told as what had happened in the Dawn times, until today. Also, not in a way where you still try to be proud of your Ancestors and a part of the people can even channel the ancestors.<br /> <br /> It is said, that there were metaphysical reasons to stop the culling - and it has been said, that Children of Gaia wanted the humans to be educated so the would not grow unchecked. The Pure Ones seem to have had that method working, while the other tribes failed massively in that undertaking, and brought their failure to the Pure ones... </div> </div> </div>Except that the Pure Ones lost more than a few of the Mound Builder peoples to the Wyrm. All was not smiles and sunshine in the pre-Colombian Americas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:43:08-07:00","id":676870,"title":"","content":"It's in the nature of the garou to be very alpha, very dominant, and this would have been even truer in ancient times. I could see a werewolf and his closer kinfold ruling over tribes like barbarian royalty, and declaring anyone who displeased them to be enemies of Gaia. You could have had a lot of Kim Jong Un situations popping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:16:12-07:00","id":676886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=676870#post676870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the nature of the garou to be very <b>alpha</b>, very dominant, and this would have been even truer in ancient times. I could see a werewolf and his closer kinfold ruling over tribes like barbarian royalty, and declaring anyone who displeased them to be enemies of Gaia. You could have had a lot of Kim Jong Un situations popping up.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YIP6EwqMEoE\" data-code=\"YIP6EwqMEoE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YIP6EwqMEoE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T21:22:40-07:00","id":677214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=675656#post675656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I tend to hold that much of the problems that the Garou now face (and endlessly b**** about) are practically direct consequences of the psychological harm done to the humans during the Impergium, and to a lesser extent, their dismissive, contemptuous attitude towards the human race in general. I'd love to play in a game where that theme gets some play -- but there's all sorts of people on this board who clearly would feel that the Garou being morally responsible for the current state of affairs in the World of Darkness (and by extension, <i>will</i> be responsible for the Apocalypse whenever it comes) is thematically, the equivalent of running your nails down a chalkboard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree with you on this point. I think this makes for the most compelling Werewolf stories, and I'd very much like to play in such a game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:56:14-07:00","id":677787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=676854#post676854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Crinos is a hell of a drug. It could also have been as simple as humans prostrating themselves and some Garou saying &quot;hey, this is pretty nice!&quot; Especially if they were born of those humans, and took their upbringing to be promise that they would eventually grow to a position of prominence and privilege, slaying monsters and coming back to reverent and tractable humans, the most attractive of whom they took as mates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there is a &quot;during a scene&quot; situation, and when we assume that there wasn't Delirium and the Curse back then, then such a situation could happen, but the other instincts of the garou like &quot;running wild and forming packs&quot; and that would in most cases prevent them to actually be tyrant rulers. Also, as rulers they would kind of have to defend their flock.<br /> <br /> So, while I see that such situations could have happened, I'm not convinced that it makes sense that there was a greater practice at work and that the tale of this practice made it into the present, but no reasoning why it happened besides &quot;our forefathers were assholes, but we admire them still&quot;. Or is the hole ancestor cult thing something that entered garou culture only after pre-history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=676854#post676854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the Pure Ones lost more than a few of the Mound Builder peoples to the Wyrm. All was not smiles and sunshine in the pre-Colombian Americas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but still they did a better job in keeping human culture close to Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=676870#post676870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the nature of the garou to be very alpha, very dominant, and this would have been even truer in ancient times. I could see a werewolf and his closer kinfold ruling over tribes like barbarian royalty, and declaring anyone who displeased them to be enemies of Gaia. You could have had a lot of Kim Jong Un situations popping up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are 3 to 5 garou in the usual pack and only one alpha - although there are some pack-less garou. And not all Garou strife to be dominant or in charge - most are perfectly fulfilled in a position amongst the pack.<br /> That said, I can see the people who ruled over this tribes in pre-history became the Silverfangs and sure, the garou members of these family-clans might be calling the shots, but that still doesn't necessarily make them tyrants terrorizing the human population.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T20:18:35-07:00","id":681713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=676729#post676729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Dawn Times already had the Litanei and it forbids to hunt humans for food, so that couldn't have been a reason to kill humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>???<br /> <br /> Um, dude, the Litany was created as part of the Concord... Y'know, <i>after</i> the Impergium. It's canon in any number of places that the Garou <i>absolutely</i> were running around eating people before that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:10:35-07:00","id":682009,"title":"","content":"The Imperigum was is another example of the Garou taking on the role of another Fera's duties. The Ratkin were in charge of that area. However subtle is not in the vocabulary of most Garou. Yes the conflict between Human and Garou is important I often use it in my own stories. It serves to reinforce the nature and dilemma of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T19:06:51-07:00","id":682581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=681713#post681713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">???<br /> <br /> Um, dude, the Litany was created as part of the Concord... Y'know, <i>after</i> the Impergium. It's canon in any number of places that the Garou <i>absolutely</i> were running around eating people before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Can't find any evidence of that in revised either.<br /> <br /> The Litany is kind of a hard topic, as the books tell us, that it is &quot;one hour long song and story epic&quot; but then tell us that local septs have rule in their Litanys that are local. Doesn't make much sense. And White Wolf/Onyx Path failed to deliver a long story anyway, or music.<br /> <br /> But there is a tale, that the garou created the Litany after the tribes had come into existence. And, as the legend goes, over decades emissaries from the tribes met, deliberated and brought the results back to their tribes, only to met again and deliberate again, for the proposals weren't agreeable for all tribes. So, the Litany only came into existence, when the garou met at a table mountain in Pangea, where as of the Umbra rules no tribal aspects remained within their personalities and they could condense al their tribal tradition into the tenets that make the Litany. Carved in stone fragments of this carvings are fetish artefacts (as per Player's Guide 1st Edition). Sure, the author ripped of Moses, but it is a great legend, declaring why the Litany is holy and something higher than tribal culture.<br /> <br /> So, while Werewolves: The Dark Ages tells us, that the Veil was proposed by the Silver Fangs and was added to the Litany in the Dark Ages this tale pretty much makes it impossible that the Concord also created the Litany - for tribal differences were the tribes was the driving force behind the end of the Impergium, and in Pangea, where the Litany was created, that would not have been possible.<br /> <br /> The Impergium also wasn't in conflict with the Litany. Killing the old, sick and weak is seen by the garou as a deed showing respect for those beneath you and their species as a whole. And if their flesh isn't eaten, the Impergium was perfectly within the limits the Litany set.<br /> <br /> So, I see the Litany as way older than the end of the Impergium.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Ratkin<br /> Yes, you are kind of right. I always wonder if the authors/game designers just didn't care about such things. I mean they came up with the Impergium to explain the Delirium. Then they thought it would be fun to bring other animals into a Player's guide - but make them antagonistic and hate garou for the most part. So, don't care that these guys get a &quot;job&quot; that is the same that garou did in the Dawn Times.<br /> <br /> But, to be fair, there isn't a mention of when each shifter breed got it's &quot;duty&quot;. The Mokol\u00e9 might have been charged with their duty early on, but who knows. Maybe the end of the Impergium and increase in numbers amongst the humans triggered the creation of the Ratkin and they hadn't had a duty before. The Kitsune origin story kind of tells us, that a shifter race an exist and not have been given a duty for an aeon or so. Also, the children of gaia TB tells us, the tribe of unicorn had explain the Ratkin how to do their job without falling to the wyrm so.<br /> <br /> Hey, what a thought, the Children of Gaia just ended the Impergium, so the rats would get a job and not be all bored all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T21:54:31-07:00","id":682642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682581#post682581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so. Can't find any evidence of that in revised either...</div> </div> </div> </div>On page 52 Silver Fangs, Lord Byeli, after going on about how the Impergium gave rise to formal tribes, and the Concord caused the political fracturing of the Garou Nation:<br /> &quot;Our tribe was most responsible for the Concord and the Litany. We could not rule all the tribes from afar, so we felt it best to give them firm guidelines with which to rule themselves...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Concord was the agreement the Silver Fangs demanded. We had divided into tribes. The Lords were to be the keepers of the ruling caste's law, called the Litany, and within each tribe, the castes became auspices.&quot; Shadow Lords, page 21.<br /> <br /> &quot;The largest and the strongest of the tribes, the Silver Fangs, called a great moot. Every Garou on Earth attended. There the Silver Fangs announced that the Impergium was ended and that there would be a Litany for all Garou. For a tenet to be included in this Litany, all of the tribes had to agree on it. And so the Garou began to decide on the tenets.&quot; Red Talons, page 20.<br /> <br /> And I know there's, like, a <i>dozen</i> other instances of this here and there, but I'm too lazy to go looking them all up right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682581#post682581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while Werewolves: The Dark Ages tells us, that the Veil was proposed by the Silver Fangs and was added to the Litany in the Dark Ages this tale pretty much makes it impossible that the Concord also created the Litany - for tribal differences were the tribes was the driving force behind the end of the Impergium, and in Pangea, where the Litany was created, that would not have been possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh* Okay, look. The Litany was created in Pangea. Yes.<br /> The inter-tribal disagreement was the driving force behind the Concord. Yes.<br /> It was also <i>why</i> they couldn't agree on anything. The Fangs moved the deliberations to Pangea to get rid of the issue of tribal-bias, <i>so they could get people on the same page</i>. They're not talking about Pangea the super-continent from Billions of years ago, they're referencing Pangea, the Umbral realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-30-2015, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T22:44:28-07:00","id":682663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682642#post682642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inter-tribal disagreement was the driving force behind the Concord. Yes.<br /> It was also <i>why</i> they couldn't agree on anything. The Fangs moved the deliberations to Pangea to get rid of the issue of tribal-bias, <i>so they could get people on the same page</i>. They're not talking about Pangea the super-continent from Billions of years ago, they're referencing Pangea, the Umbral realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pangea-on-earth was 'only' 300 million years ago, but yours is still an excellent point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T00:11:56-07:00","id":682723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682642#post682642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 52 Silver Fangs, Lord Byeli, after going on about how the Impergium gave rise to formal tribes, and the Concord caused the political fracturing of the Garou Nation:<br /> &amp;quot;Our tribe was most responsible for the Concord and the Litany. We could not rule all the tribes from afar, so we felt it best to give them firm guidelines with which to rule themselves...&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The Concord was the agreement the Silver Fangs demanded. We had divided into tribes. The Lords were to be the keepers of the ruling caste's law, called the Litany, and within each tribe, the castes became auspices.&amp;quot; Shadow Lords, page 21.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The largest and the strongest of the tribes, the Silver Fangs, called a great moot. Every Garou on Earth attended. There the Silver Fangs announced that the Impergium was ended and that there would be a Litany for all Garou. For a tenet to be included in this Litany, all of the tribes had to agree on it. And so the Garou began to decide on the tenets.&amp;quot; Red Talons, page 20.<br /> <br /> And I know there's, like, a <i>dozen</i> other instances of this here and there, but I'm too lazy to go looking them all up right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> *sigh* Okay, look. The Litany was created in Pangea. Yes.<br /> The inter-tribal disagreement was the driving force behind the Concord. Yes.<br /> It was also <i>why</i> they couldn't agree on anything. The Fangs moved the deliberations to Pangea to get rid of the issue of tribal-bias, <i>so they could get people on the same page</i>. They're not talking about Pangea the super-continent from Billions of years ago, they're referencing Pangea, the Umbral realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little fuzzy on when did the tribes form. I thought they were only formalized after the Impergium as different forms of reactions to the Concord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T00:39:38-07:00","id":682728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682642#post682642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not talking about Pangea the super-continent from Billions of years ago, they're referencing Pangea, the Umbral realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you telling me this, I already pointed out, that &quot;Umbra rules&quot; apply, specifically the rules of the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682642#post682642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not talking about Pangea the super-continent from Billions of years ago, they're referencing Pangea, the Umbral realm.*sigh* Okay, look. The Litany was created in Pangea. Yes.<br /> The inter-tribal disagreement was the driving force behind the Concord. Yes.<br /> It was also <i>why</i> they couldn't agree on anything. The Fangs moved the deliberations to Pangea to get rid of the issue of tribal-bias, <i>so they could get people on the same page</i>. They're not talking about Pangea the super-continent from Billions of years ago, they're referencing Pangea, the Umbral realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legends about the end of the Impergium clearly state different tribes and their opinions. Specifically Children of Gaia, Red Talons, Shadowlords, Silver Fangs and Stargazer. So, in Pangea, as per page 78 of Umbra revised, they would not only forget their tribal differences, but also be not identifiable as members of any given tribe.<br /> So, ending the Impergium there, in the umbra, would not really have lead to the tale, that a Silver Fang lost a contest of gamecraft to a Stargazer - bit merely that one garou from each side participated in a contest and the faction that wanted to end the Impergium won.<br /> In any case there was hasn't been a mention of the end of the Impergium specifically happening in Pangea, and the whole legend about the Red Talons forming in that instant would be pointless in Pangea.<br /> <br /> None of your quotes stated that Impergium's end and the creation of the Litany fell to the same instant in time. The Red Talon quote merely states, the Silver Fangs announced both at a grand moot, suggesting that the Litany came into existence after the Impergium's end. However, the same quote can also be understood as the Silver Fangs reinforcing that the Litany was binding to all tribes and calling upon &quot;Submit to those of higher station&quot;, making their disputed decision to end the Impergium a command.<br /> <br /> The information you read from the quotes isn't actually written there, and there are logical difficulties if both aspects of the garou history happened at the same time. Mentioning both in the same paragraph is not uncommon if one details tribal history, since they both occurred in the Dawn Times. But that could mean that there were a thousand years between both, or mere decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:22:24-07:00","id":682788,"title":"","content":"You're discussing oral lore. None of it's bound to be exactly reliable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T02:34:01-07:00","id":682852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682788#post682788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're discussing oral lore. None of it's bound to be exactly reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Hence discussing it, like Galliards of different tribes would. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T06:19:22-07:00","id":683052,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know, but you two seem to be disagreeing, and it does bear reminding that such details have corraboration to go both your ways (and a few others as well). We just don't know what the exact history was prior to humans actually trying to keep a touch of history. Heck, even with all our attempts to record &quot;objectivley&quot; all our knowledge of history is biased and skewed, for oral cultures its even worse, since the stories become gospel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T06:46:39-07:00","id":683065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682663#post682663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pangea-on-earth was 'only' 300 million years ago, but yours is still an excellent point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> AKA 290 million years before humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:38:07-07:00","id":683478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/675469-garou-nation-vs-humanity?p=682723#post682723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little fuzzy on when did the tribes form. I thought they were only formalized after the Impergium as different forms of reactions to the Concord.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many mentioned of members of different tribes regarding their actions to end or keep the Impergium. Could be, that they were proto-Garou and only associated with tribes after the fact, but I somehow doubt it. I think the tribes formed due to the garou's spread over the world and cultures starting to grow separately.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}